The attached image (Figure 2 from the npj Vaccines 2017 paper) illustrates the biodistribution and clearance of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 after intramuscular injection in mice over 21 days. Panel A shows whole-mouse fluorescence imaging, revealing that Nano-11 remains largely localized at the injection site with a gradual decrease in intensity over time. Panel B confirms that internal organs show minimal to no fluorescent signal by day 21, indicating no systemic distribution. Panel C quantifies the injection site fluorescence, showing a rapid initial decrease, followed by a transient increase on day 2, and then a steady decline, with only about 20% of the original signal remaining by day 21.